@startuml
' What: where LLMs sit around the game today (D-26 ... D-30) and in a later version (§6).
' Shows: the advisor is the player's own LLM project with a one-way paste; rivals are code an LLM wrote from the rulebook;
'        concepts come from a library an LLM generated at development time.
' Source: brainstorming-base.md, D-26, D-27, D-28, D-29, D-30, §6 (later version).
title LLMs around the game (D-26 ... D-30)
actor "Human player" as HP
component "SYNTROPY" as G
component "Player's own LLM project\n(advisor kit, persona with a profile)" as ADV
component "Rival code\n(written by an LLM from the rulebook)" as RIV
component "Concept library\n(generated by an LLM at dev time)" as LIB
G --> HP : player view
HP --> ADV : one-way paste (optional)
ADV --> HP : advice, never parsed by the game
HP --> G : picks, builds, research
RIV --> G : most / least picks
LIB --> G : concepts, priced by the Valuation Engine
note bottom of RIV : Later version: LLMs play rivals live\nand invent concepts (§6)
@enduml
